Any person charged with violating this Code or any ordinance of the city or any state traffic law is entitled to be released as follows:
(1) Copy of charges. Any person may be released, at the discretion of the arresting officer or other authorized officer, on signing a copy of charges, unless otherwise established by law or court order.
(2) Posting cash bail. Any person shall be released upon posting the required cash bail as set forth in the cash bond schedule.
(3) Property bond. Any property owner within the city may serve as the security for their personal appearance or the personal appearance of any other person in municipal court, provided equity exceeds the cash bond by more than twice the amount of the cash bond and there are no other property bonds outstanding. A copy of the deed to the property pledged shall be sufficient proof of ownership.
(4) Professional bonding company. Any professional bondsmen licensed to do business in the city or their employees of record may sign a bond in an amount not to exceed ten percent of the principal amount for any person's personal appearance in municipal court, provided such bondsmen maintain their businesses in accordance with the professional bonding requirements of this Code.
(5) Military bond. Any member of the military forces of the United States may be, at their request, released to the nearest military unit until their appearance in municipal court.
(6) Referral bond. Any property owner outside the city may serve as the security for their personal appearance or the personal appearance of any other person in municipal court, provided equity exceeds the cash bond by more than twice the amount of the cash bond and there are no other property bonds outstanding. Such bond shall be made through the sheriff's office in the county where the property deed is recorded.
(7) Driver's license bond. Any person possessing a valid state driver's license may surrender such driver's license in lieu of bond for any violation of a state traffic law, except for:
a. Driving under the influence of alcohol or drugs (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-391);
b. Driving with driver's license in suspension or revocation (O.C.G.A. § 40-5-121);
c. Fleeing or attempting to elude police (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-395(a));
d. Impersonating a law enforcement officer (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-395(c));
e. Racing on highways or streets (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-186(b));
f. Any leaving the scene of an accident violation (O.C.G.A. §§ 40-6-270(a), 40-6-272, 40-6-273);
g. Reckless driving (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-390(a));
h. Laying drags (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-251(a)); and
i. Homicide by vehicle in the second degree (O.C.G.A. § 40-6-393(b)), unless otherwise provided for by law; or
j. By order of the presiding judge, chief of police or any person authorized to act in their behalf.
(8) Driver's license bond; misdemeanor ordinance violations. Any person possessing a valid state driver's license may surrender such driver's license in lieu of bond for any violation of an ordinance, when such person has been incarcerated in the city jail for a minimum of five days.
(Code 1977, § 8-6; Ord. No. 93-09, § 8-6, 9-20-93)
